# LCEDA schematic work

When a task creates, edits, redraws, cleans up, reviews, or beautifies an LCEDA schematic, load `lceda-draw-readable-schematic` first and its directed companion skills.

Hard rules:
- Discover the actual `lceda_mcp_server` tool schemas and read the active target before writes. Never invent tool names/arguments/UUIDs/nets/pins.
- Verify the active document is a schematic. LCEDA schematic coordinates are 10mil per unit; do not reuse PCB coordinate assumptions.
- Before routing, read actual component pin geometry. Choose component orientation from `0/90/180/270°` candidates; mirror only with a real reason.
- Placement precedes routing. Series path parts normally align with signal flow; decoupling/pull/divider branches normally follow vertical power semantics.
- Finished wires are orthogonal. 0–2 bends is normal, 3 is warning, local 4+ bends fails and returns to placement/abstraction.
- Use Wire for local topology, a real same-sheet Label for non-local identity, Port for sheet/module boundaries, and NetFlag for power/ground. Never fake a missing Label using Port/text.
- Never force `SCH_PrimitiveWire.create(..., net)` just to make a connection succeed; explicit net can propagate to touching unnamed primitives.
- For beautification, preserve electrical topology and use three passes: Orientation → Alignment/spacing → Wiring/label.
- Do not declare completion until Netlist/DRC and geometry hard gates pass, or unsupported checks are explicitly reported.
